{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.QSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Formal"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.identity_holds_in_realification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.identity_holds_in_realification","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L150-L157","doc":"**Statement-level F_p reduction commutes with realification**\nin the sense that any polynomial identity holding in\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (and hence in every F_p[q, q⁻¹]) realifies\nto the same identity in ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement_smul","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L131-L140","doc":"**Realification commutes with scalar multiplication** by\na formal Laurent polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement_add","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L121-L129","doc":"**Realification commutes with addition**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyHeckeElement","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L114-L119","doc":"**Element-wise realification** of a `HeckeFormalElement ℤ n`\nat `q_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyZ","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**Realification at q_0** of an integer formal Laurent\npolynomial: embed ℤ → ℝ, then eval at q_0.\n\nUniform for all primes: any congruence/identity in\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (and its F_p reductions) maps coherently to ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.embedIntToReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.embedIntToReal","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L92-L100","doc":"**Embed ℤ-coefficient Laurent polynomials into ℝ**.\n\nMathlib API drift: the coefficient-map ring hom on\n`LaurentPolynomial R = AddMonoidAlgebra R ℤ` is\n`AddMonoidAlgebra.mapRangeRingHom`; the former\n`LaurentPolynomial.mapRingHom` no longer resolves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyAtRealQ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Realification.realifyAtRealQ0","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Realification.lean#L73-L83","doc":"**Realification of a formal Laurent polynomial at q_0**.\n\nFor `f ∈ ℝ[q, q⁻¹]`, `realifyAt q_0 f = f(q_0) ∈ ℝ`.\n\nUses Mathlib's `LaurentPolynomial.eval₂RingHom` with the\nidentity coefficient embedding and `q_0` as the evaluation\nvalue (must be a unit; here `q_0 ≠ 0` from `q_0 > 1` gives\n`IsUnit q_0` in the field ℝ). ","signatureChunk":0}]}